Akurion is a fictional location created by the late American author Howard Phillips Lovecraft for his 1920 short story "The Doom That Came to Sarnath."

### Overview
Akurion is the name given by the people of the city of Sarnath to a tall grey rock that served as a tidal marker near the shore of the unnamed lake where Sarnath once stood. (: "The Doom That Came to Sarnath")

: "The House on Curwen Street"
|created by=August Derleth
}}


An Investigation into the Myth-Patterns of Latter-day Primitives with Especial Reference to the R’lyeh Text is a fictional scholarly work created by August Derleth, attributed to his character Laban Shrewsbury.

It first appeared in Derleth's story "The House on Curwen Street" (1944) and is also mentioned in his The Lurker at the Threshold (1945), "The Gorge Beyond Salapunco" (1949), and "The Keeper of the Key" (1951).

The book also figures in Lin Carter's "The Horror in the Gallery."

: "The Diary of Alonzo Typer"
|created by = Howard Phillips Lovecraft and William Lumley
}}


An Ancient One is a humanoid that has squid-like features and exists only partly in the physical, material dimension.

: The Shadow Out of Time
 | created by     = H. P. Lovecraft
 }}

The arachnid denizens of Earth's last age are a fictional species created by H. P. Lovecraft for his novella The Shadow Out of Time.

### Description
Nothing is known about this species except that they inhabit Earth in a distant future, long after the extinction of humanity and of the coleopteran race that followed it. By the time of the arachnids, the Earth will be a cold, inhospitable planet, and the natives will be forced to move to underground burrows to survive. At least two members of this species were abducted by the Great Race of Yith and were met by Nathaniel Wingate Peaslee. (: The Shadow Out of Time)

