### Description
The Dark One is a telepathic alien creature from an extradimensional realm that the writer Edgar Henquist Gordon made contact with in his dreams. It appears in the form of a black furred creature with claws, fangs, green eyes, and a porcine snout. Gordon claimed that the Dark One and his kin were "forces that once were manifested physically on Earth" in the Middle Ages, and that its physical appearance reflects what the people believed a demon would look like.

However, Gordon was adamant in his belief that the Dark One wasn't evil, just an alien creature feared by superstitious humans. He went as far as to describe the Dark One as "a superior intelligence who wishes to gain mental rapport with human minds" and establish trade between the people of Earth and "Those beyond". The Dark One instructed Gordon to write books of fiction told from the perspective of alien minds. Gordon did so, even though the books' subjects turned out to be so horrifying as to alienate audiences and be rejected by publishers. After agreeing to become one with the entity, Gordon was possessed and his body assumed the form of the Dark Demon. A friend who met him in this condition was so terrified that he shot him. After death, Gordon's body vanished completely, leaving only his clothes behind. (: "The Dark Demon")

