Jean Grenier is a fictional character created by H. P. Lovecraft for his comedy short story "Ibid".

### Biography
Jean Grenier was a 17th century French trader operating in New England. In 1683, he saw the skull of Ibidus, which had been bought from the local Pequots by Dutch fur-trader Petrus van Schaack. A fervent Catholic who venerated Ibidus as "St. Ibide", Grenier was enraged by the sight of the relic in the hands of a Protestant. As a result, he murdered van Schaack, crushing his head with an axe, and fled to the north, taking the skull with him. On the way, Grenier himself was robbed and killed by the voyageur Michel Savard, who added the skull to his own collection. (: "Ibid")

