Thornton is a fictional character created by H. P. Lovecraft for his horror short story "The Rats in the Walls".

### Biography
Thornton was a psychic investigator who took part in the 1923 expedition to explore the ancient catacombs beneath Exham Priory, along with Delapore, Edward Norrys, Sir William Brinton, Dr. Trask, and two other scholars. A particularly sensitive man, Thornton fainted twice during the ordeal, first when he saw the massive subterranean grotto in the interior of the cliff, which was covered with ancient ruins and blanketed by human and humanoid bones, and again when Trask told him that some of the skeletons must have belonged to human lineages that became quadrupedal over the course of several generations. These quadrupedal humans were raised as livestock for centuries by the cannibal members of certain cults, which included Delapore's ancestors. Whether due to the psychic influence of supernatural forces or more mundane mental breakdown, the experience proved too much for Thornton and he ended up interred in Hanwell Asylum along with Delapore. (: "The Rats in the Walls")

